From 121f397f6854b186221032b57292049b57ef5df1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds-bootstrap <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:57:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Nintendo WFC unused session: drop static where the header
 declares the state functions

include/nintendo_wfc_connect_unused.h declares the 57
NintendoWfcUnused_AskConnect ... NintendoWfcUnused_WaitErrorDismiss state
functions without static, but src/nintendo_wfc_connect_unused_session.c
repeats them as static forward declarations (:41-98) and definitions. GCC
rejects each with "static declaration ... follows non-static declaration"
(57 errors). MWCC kept the file-scope symbols local and never compared them
with the header. Same fix as 1512/1523: NINTENDO_WFC_FILE_SCOPE expands to
nothing under SDK_PORT_3DS so the definitions match the header, and to static
on the DS so the original text and linkage are unchanged.

gcc-10 -E -P without SDK_PORT_3DS: byte-identical (449316 bytes both).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nintendo_wfc_connect_unused_session.c | 237 +++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 123 insertions(+), 114 deletions(-)

